  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "A small, rich force focused on defending a peninsula with critical gas infrastructure (Ras Laffan) and the large US air base at Al Udeid. The Emiri Land Force has been rebuilt since 2015 with German armour (Leopard 2A7+, PzH 2000, Boxer, Fennek, Dingo) and a large Turkish MRAP fleet, with a Turkish brigade-size presence and training mission in the country. Real ground-combat experience is limited; strength is in air defence, ISR and partnership. Qatar's diplomatic role is mediation (Gaza ceasefire talks, US-Taliban talks, hosting the Hamas political office), and it was struck both by Israel (September 2025, Doha) and by Iran (2026, including Ras Laffan and Hamad International Airport) while declaring itself not a party to the Iran war.",
    "squad_size": 8,
    "fireteam": "Western-style section of 8 in two fireteams, mounted in Ejder Yalçın or Boxer; special forces (Emiri Guard and Internal Security Force Lekhwiya) in teams of 4-8. In game: 8 men in battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Static defence of key infrastructure (gas plants, ports, airports) with layered counter-drone and air defence",
      "Mobile MRAP quick-reaction forces patrolling the coast",
      "Joint operations with Turkish and US forces stationed in the country",
      "Leopard 2A7+ and PzH 2000 as a high-end deterrent rather than an expeditionary tool"
    ],
